    "updated": "2026-11-05",
    "answer": "A copy-and-run Node module that checks a webhook signature from Oura, WHOOP, Terra or Polar on your server, each the way the vendor's own page describes it. All four use HMAC-SHA256, and no two sign the same string: Oura signs the timestamp header plus JSON.stringify of the parsed body and sends upper-case hex, WHOOP signs the millisecond timestamp plus the raw body and sends base64, Terra signs timestamp, a period and the raw body inside a t=…,v1=… header, and Polar signs the raw body alone. Its test suite signs with this file and verifies with the module behind /tools/webhook-verifier, and the other way round, for every vendor.",
